e=A.ce(A.a7(["Python",'# Insert a value at a specific index by shifting elements right\ndef insert_at(arr, size, index, value, capacity):\n    if size >= capacity:\n        return "Array is full!"\n    # Shift from the end down to the insert index\n    for i in range(size - 1, index - 1, -1):\n        arr[i + 1] = arr[i]\n    arr[index] = value\n    return size + 1  # new size\n',"Java","// Insert value at given index\nvoid insertAt(int[] arr, int size, int index, int value) {\n    // Shift elements right from the end\n    for (int i = size - 1; i >= index; i--) {\n        arr[i + 1] = arr[i];\n    }\n    arr[index] = value;\n    // Remember to increment size in the caller\n}\n","C++",'#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int arr[6] = {12, 22, 45, 74, 36};\n    int size = 5, index = 2, value = 99;\n    for (int i = size - 1; i >= index; i--) {\n        arr[i + 1] = arr[i];\n    }\n    arr[index] = value;\n    size++;\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) cout << arr[i] << " ";\n    return 0;\n}\n',"JavaScript","// Insert value at index in a fixed-size simulation\nfunction insertAt(arr, size, index, value) {\n    for (let i = size - 1; i >= index; i--) {\n        arr[i + 1] = arr[i];  // shift right\n    }\n    arr[index] = value;\n    return size + 1;\n}\n"],d,d),p,q,"Insertion adds a new element at a specific position in an array. While appending to the end is instant (O(1)), inserting anywhere else requires shifting all subsequent elements to the right to maintain order \u2014 making it an O(n) operation. Understanding the shift direction and capacity constraints is essential.","array-insertion",m,"Array Insertion",A.a(["Shifting from the front instead of the back overwrites data before saving it","Forgetting to check capacity before inserting \u2014 causes data loss in fixed arrays","Off-by-one in the shift loop: should include the insert index, not stop before it"],h),e,A.a([A.a0(1,"You must start at the back of the array and pull elements to the right. If you start at the insertion index and push right, you will overwrite the next element before you have a chance to move it!",A.a(["From the insertion index moving to the right.","From the very end of the array moving down to the insertion index.","From the beginning of the array moving to the left.","You do not need to shift elements; they automatically make room."],h),"When inserting an element into the middle of an array, in which direction must you shift the existing elements?"),A.a0(2,"The worst-case scenario is inserting an element at the very beginning (index 0). Every single existing element in the array must be shifted one position to the right, which takes O(n) time.",A.a(["O(1)","O(log n)","O(n)","O(n\xb2)"],h),"What is the worst-case time complexity for inserting an element into a standard array?"),A.a0(1,"Fixed-size arrays cannot grow. If you try to insert a new item into an array that is already at maximum capacity, your program will crash or overwrite unowned memory.",A.a(["If the array is sorted.","If the array has reached its maximum capacity.","If the value is a positive number.","If the array contains duplicate values."],h),"What is the very first thing you must check before attempting to insert a new element into a fixed-size array?"),A.a0(0,"If there is available capacity, appending to the end requires zero shifting. You simply place the item in the next empty slot, which is an instant O(1) operation.",A.a(["O(1)","O(n)","O(n log n)","O(2^n)"],h),"Inserting an element at the very end of an array (appending) usually takes what time complexity?")],c),"assets/mds/dsa/array/array_insertion.md",B.SG)
